// ============================================================================
// METADATA
// ============================================================================
//
// # M.1 Core Identity [IDENTITY]
//
//	Key:         B-void-workflow-file-creation
//	Scripture:   "In all labour there is profit" — Proverbs 14:23
//	Principle:   Template-first creation ensures structural DNA carries forward
//	Anchor:      "A workman that needeth not to be ashamed" — 2 Timothy 2:15
//
//	Type:        Rails — infrastructure pattern for file creation
//	Role:        Defines how new files are created from templates
//	Dependency:  DEPENDED — references word/seed/ templates
//
//	Architect:   Nova Dawn
//	Created:     2025-12-11
//	Version:     a-01.00
//
//	Becomes:     word/standards/workflows/file-creation.jsonc when proven
//
// # M.2 Version History [HISTORY]
//
//   - a-01.00 (2025-12-11) — Initial capture of file creation patterns
//   - a-01.01 (2025-12-25) — Updated to 3-block structure with numbered sections
//
// # M.3 Interface [INTERFACE]
//
//	Consumer:  Nova Dawn, team members, create-from-template skill
//	Loader:    Human reading, skill invocation
//	Depends:   word/seed/ templates, glossary (boundary-marker, block-by-block)
//	Pattern:   Read workflow → identify file type → cp template → fill blocks
//
// # M.4 Operational [OPERATIONAL]
//
//	Blocking:  no (-1) — workflow documentation, not executable
//	Health:    N/A — human-consumed documentation
//
//	Status:    void (capturing patterns) — moves to word/ when proven
//
